    intro: "When Jesus was on trial before the high priest, he said something that sealed his condemnation: 'From now on you will see the Son of Man seated at the right hand of Power and coming on the clouds of heaven.' He was claiming that he would be vindicated and would return in glory. The disciples remembered his words. Forty days after the resurrection, as they watched him rise into the sky, two angels asked them why they were staring, and told them that this same Jesus would come in the same way.",
    context: "Throughout his ministry Jesus spoke of coming again. He compared himself to a master returning from a journey, a bridegroom arriving at midnight, a thief coming in the night and a king coming in glory with his angels. At his trial he quoted Daniel 7, where one like a son of man comes with the clouds of heaven and receives everlasting dominion. The high priest tore his robes and called it blasphemy, for he understood that Jesus was claiming to be the divine Son of Man.",
